  "weld-in-saddle-female-thread": {
    "seo_p1": "The weld-in saddle with female thread (Weld-in Saddle Female Thread) combines the advantages of fast saddle installation with a direct metal connection.",
    "seo_p2": "In addition to the PP-R saddle body, this fitting features a firmly anchored brass female thread that provides an extremely twist-resistant base for valves.",
    "seo_p3": "Ideal for the subsequent installation of drain valves, air vents or measuring sensors directly into existing main lines without time-consuming pipe network separation.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What is the main advantage of this weld-in saddle?",
        "a": "It enables the direct installation of a metal female thread on an existing pipeline, which is extremely time and space saving."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can thermometers be screwed in here?",
        "a": "Yes, the saddle is the ideal interface for integrating temperature sensors or small pressure gauges permanently and pressure-tight into heating networks."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is the brass thread protected from tearing out?",
        "a": "Absolutely. The brass insert is injected deep into the PP-R structure and anchored mechanically inseparably by special knurling."
      }
    ]
  },
  "weld-in-saddle-male-thread": {
    "seo_p1": "The weld-in saddle with male thread (Weld-in Saddle Male Thread) allows the immediate connection of system components with union nuts to a base pipe.",
    "seo_p2": "The seamlessly welded PP-R saddle carries a solid brass male thread that withstands highest leverage forces and permanent temperature changes.",
    "seo_p3": "This component is frequently used in manifold construction to mount shut-off valves or pump outlets extremely space-savingly and aerodynamically.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "For which connections is the male thread on the saddle suitable?",
        "a": "It is optimally suited for the direct connection of fittings with female threads or for connections secured with a union nut."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is this saddle available for all pipe dimensions?",
        "a": "The weld-in saddle is available for main pipes from 40 mm to 125 mm, with the male thread typically being 1/2\" or 3/4\"."
      },
      {
        "q": "How is the tightness ensured after drilling?",
        "a": "The fusing of the saddle and pipe creates a cohesive, homogeneous connection that is 100% tight at the molecular level."
      }
    ]
  },
  "pipe-clamps": {
    "seo_p1": "The pipe clamps form the mechanical foundation for standardized and durable fastening of PP-R piping systems.",
    "seo_p2": "Equipped with sound-decoupling rubber inserts and sturdy steel hinges, these clamps safely absorb the thermal linear expansion of the pipe.",
    "seo_p3": "They are absolutely essential to fix pipe runs to walls or ceilings and to effectively isolate pipe noise from the building structure.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What is the rubber insert in the clamp for?",
        "a": "The EPDM insert serves for sound decoupling according to DIN 4109 and prevents the transmission of flow noise to the masonry."
      },
      {
        "q": "Should the clamp be mounted as a fixed point or sliding point?",
        "a": "Depending on the tightening torque of the screws, the clamp can be used both as a fixing fixed point and as a sliding sliding point for thermal linear expansion."
      },
      {
        "q": "What thread connection do the pipe clamps have?",
        "a": "Our standard pipe clamps have a welded combination nut (M8/M10), which allows flexible fastening to common hanger bolts or threaded rods."
      }
    ]
  },
  "backing-flange-pp-steel-sfbf": {
    "seo_p1": "The PP/Steel backing flange (Backing Flange PP/Steel SFBF) ensures a highly resilient and dimensionally stable flange connection for large pipe diameters.",
    "seo_p2": "A steel core, completely coated with robust polypropylene (PP), completely prevents corrosion and prevents bending under high contact pressure.",
    "seo_p3": "This accessory is crucial for the transition to large pumps or steel tanks in industrial plants, where extreme tensile forces must be safely dissipated.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Why is the steel core coated with polypropylene?",
        "a": "The plastic coating permanently protects the high-strength steel from corrosion, which is particularly crucial in damp basements or aggressive industrial environments."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the hole pattern meet standard norms?",
        "a": "Yes, the drilling pattern of our backing flanges is exactly aligned with the European DIN EN 1092-1 standard and fits all standard counter flanges."
      },
      {
        "q": "Do the screws have to be tightened with a torque wrench?",
        "a": "We strongly recommend cross-tightening with a calibrated torque wrench to ensure uniform compression of the seal."
      }
    ]
  },
  "flat-gasket": {
    "seo_p1": "The flat gasket is the essential sealing element for all flange connections within our PP-R system.",
    "seo_p2": "Punched from high-quality EPDM or other elastomers, the gasket is specially tailored to the smooth end faces of the flange adapters and withstands high mains pressure.",
    "seo_p3": "It compensates for microscopic unevenness and ensures a 100% leak-free and durable connection for flange transitions in industry or heating technology.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What material is the flat gasket made of?",
        "a": "By default, our flange gaskets are made of high-pressure-resistant EPDM, which is excellently suited for drinking water and heating water."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can the gasket be reused?",
        "a": "No, for safety reasons a new flat gasket must always be used after a flange connection has been loosened."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is the gasket resistant to chemicals?",
        "a": "EPDM offers good resistance to many aqueous solutions. For specific industrial chemicals, please check our resistance lists beforehand."
      }
    ]
  },
  "flat-gasket-for-unions-pp-r": {
    "seo_p1": "The flat gasket for unions (Flat Gasket for Unions PP-R) is precisely dimensioned for our plastic and metal unions.",
    "seo_p2": "The elastomer material, approved for drinking water, offers a high restoring force and is resistant to permanent thermal loads in hot water networks.",
    "seo_p3": "Regular replacement of this gasket after maintenance work on valves or pumps guarantees the permanent tightness of the screw connection.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "How tight can the union be tightened?",
        "a": "To avoid destroying the seal, the union nut should be tightened hand-tight and then only slightly (approx. 1/4 turn) with a tool."
      },
      {
        "q": "Are these gaskets also available in other materials?",
        "a": "For extreme temperature requirements or special industrial media, we can also offer gaskets made of FKM (Viton) or PTFE upon request."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does this gasket fit on other brands?",
        "a": "It is tailor-made for the tongue and groove design of K Aqua unions, but can also be used for other unions with the same dimensions."
      }
    ]
  },
  "plug": {
    "seo_p1": "The plug serves for the temporary or permanent closing of open threaded connections in sanitary installations.",
    "seo_p2": "Injection-molded from stable PP-R and often provided with an integrated sealing ring, the plug withstands the full test pressure during system acceptance.",
    "seo_p3": "It protects the piping system from dirt during the construction phase and reliably seals wall plates until the final assembly of the outlet fittings.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Does the plug withstand the water pressure during the construction phase?",
        "a": "Yes, it is designed to withstand the full test pressure (often more than 15 bar) during the pressure test of the pipe network."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the plug have to be additionally sealed with Teflon?",
        "a": "Our plugs usually have an integrated O-ring, so no additional sealing tape such as Teflon or hemp is required."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can the plug remain permanently in the wall?",
        "a": "It is primarily designed as a construction plug. For permanent blind closures, we recommend corresponding brass blind plugs."
      }
    ]
  },
  "pipe-cutter-2040": {
    "seo_p1": "The pipe cutter d20-d40 (Pipe Cutter 20-40) is the indispensable precision tool for clean cross-cuts on small to medium pipe dimensions.",
    "seo_p2": "Equipped with a titanium-coated blade and mechanical leverage, the shears guarantee an absolutely right-angled cut through PP-R pipes without material deformation.",
    "seo_p3": "A clean, burr-free cut is the basic prerequisite for a standardized and durable welded connection. This tool is the constant companion of every installer.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Why is a special pipe cutter so important?",
        "a": "A right-angled and burr-free cut without crushing is absolutely imperative to ensure a perfect, void-free welded connection."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can the blade be replaced?",
        "a": "Yes, in the event of wear or damage, the high-strength steel blade can easily be replaced with an original spare part."
      },
      {
        "q": "Do the shears also work in cold temperatures?",
        "a": "The power transmission always works, however the PP-R pipe should not be cut at freezing temperatures, as it could splinter."
      }
    ]
  },
  "pipe-cutter-50125": {
    "seo_p1": "The large pipe cutter d50-d125 (Pipe Cutter 50-125) is a robust roller cutting tool for large-volume plastic pipes.",
    "seo_p2": "Its solid steel body and specially hardened cutting wheel effortlessly penetrate thick pipe walls of the large SDR classes with absolute plane parallelism.",
    "seo_p3": "Ideal for the preparation of main distribution lines in industrial construction, this cutter prevents stress-induced cracks that could occur with simple saw cuts.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "How does cutting such thick pipes work?",
        "a": "The tool is clamped around the pipe, the cutting wheel is slowly advanced and the cutter is guided around the pipe in even turning movements."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does this tool also cut fiber composite pipes?",
        "a": "Yes, the specially hardened cutting wheel also cuts through our glass fiber reinforced PPRCT pipes effortlessly and extremely precisely."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the roller cutter replace chamfering?",
        "a": "Socket welding requires no chamfering. The absolutely straight cut of this tool is the perfect preparation for the welding process."
      }
    ]
  },
  "pipe-cutter-50125-1": {
    "seo_p1": "The high-performance pipe cutter d50-d125 V1 (Pipe Cutter 50-125-1) is a modified version for particularly fast and ergonomic cuts.",
    "seo_p2": "With an optimized spindle guide and an integrated quick-return mechanism, it enormously accelerates the cutting process of massive PP-R pipes.",
    "seo_p3": "Designed for construction projects with high pipe consumption from 50 mm diameter, this tool reduces the physical strain on the user to a minimum.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What does 'quick-return mechanism' mean?",
        "a": "After completion of the cut, the cutting wheel can be immediately returned to the starting position at the push of a button, without tedious cranking back."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is this model better suited for stationary use?",
        "a": "It is mobile, but thanks to its massive design and precise spindle guide, it can be excellently used for stationary prefabrication."
      },
      {
        "q": "Are there spare parts for this pipe cutter?",
        "a": "Yes, both the cutting wheel and the guide rollers are permanently available as original spare parts."
      }
    ]
  }

"hand-welding-machine-2032-complete-set": {
    "seo_p1": "The hand welding machine d20-d32 in a complete set (Hand Welding Machine 20-32 Complete Set) is the professional base station for small dimensions.",
    "seo_p2": "It includes a thermostatically controlled 800-watt heating element, Teflon-coated welding tools and a stable stand in a robust metal case.",
    "seo_p3": "Designed for fast and standardized pre-wall and floor installation, the device keeps the required welding temperature of 260°C absolutely constant at all times.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Why is an electronic thermostat so important?",
        "a": "Only a precise thermostat guarantees the DVS-compliant permanent temperature of exactly 260°C, which is absolutely necessary for a safe PP-R fusion."
      },
      {
        "q": "How long does the heating phase take?",
        "a": "Thanks to the powerful 800-watt heating element, the device usually reaches the operating temperature in under 10 minutes."
      },
      {
        "q": "Which tools are included in the case?",
        "a": "The set includes the heating device, the stand, Teflon mandrels for 20, 25 and 32 mm, Allen key and mounting screws in a steel case."
      }
    ]
  },
  "hand-welding-machine-2063-complete-set": {
    "seo_p1": "The hand welding machine d20-d63 in a complete set (Hand Welding Machine 20-63 Complete Set) covers the entire range of classic building services.",
    "seo_p2": "With a higher heating output and double slots for heating mandrels, this device enables the simultaneous preparation of different dimensions without changing tools.",
    "seo_p3": "The robust complete set is designed for the rough everyday life on the construction site and delivers an uncompromisingly precise welding temperature even in adverse weather conditions.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Can several welding tools be mounted at the same time?",
        "a": "Yes, the wide heating sword head allows the simultaneous mounting of up to three heating mandrel pairs for uninterrupted work."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the device give a signal when the temperature is reached?",
        "a": "A clearly visible indicator light signals to the user as soon as the operating temperature of 260°C has been reached and stabilized."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is the device suitable for continuous operation on large construction sites?",
        "a": "Absolutely. The durable heating element and heat-resistant wiring are specially designed for industrial shift operation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "hand-welding-machine-mirror-50125": {
    "seo_p1": "The hand welding machine with mirror d50-d125 (Hand Welding Machine Mirror 50-125) has been specially developed for large socket welds.",
    "seo_p2": "An extremely flat, large-area heating mirror guarantees the even heating of solid fittings and pipes. The output of over 1200 watts ensures fast heating phases.",
    "seo_p3": "Absolutely essential for the manual processing of large supply lines in industry, where temperature drops during the welding process would be catastrophic.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Why is a flat mirror required for large pipes?",
        "a": "Large diameters (from 50 mm) have an enormous mass. The flat mirror provides an extremely large contact area to bring the heat quickly and evenly into the plastic."
      },
      {
        "q": "How heavy is the device?",
        "a": "Despite its high performance, the device is ergonomically balanced, but for pipes from 90 mm it usually requires two installers for exact joining."
      },
      {
        "q": "Do the Teflon-coated surfaces have to be cleaned?",
        "a": "Yes, they should be carefully cleaned after each use while still warm with a lint-free paper towel or a special wooden spatula."
      }
    ]
  },
  "welding-tool": {
    "seo_p1": "The welding tools (Welding Tool) are the Teflon-coated heating mandrels and heating sockets that take over the actual melting of the PP-R material.",
    "seo_p2": "Made of highly thermally conductive alloys and provided with a special non-stick PTFE coating, they guarantee a perfect, residue-free molecular melt.",
    "seo_p3": "Only with undamaged and high-quality welding tools can the homogeneity of the connection required by the DVS for a 50-year service life be achieved.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "When must a welding tool be replaced?",
        "a": "As soon as the Teflon coating is scratched or PP-R residues burn firmly, the tool must be replaced in order to avoid faulty weld seams."
      },
      {
        "q": "Why am I not allowed to scrape off plastic residues with a knife?",
        "a": "A knife immediately destroys the micro-fine PTFE non-stick coating. Use only soft cloths on the still hot tool."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the K Aqua welding tool also fit on third-party devices?",
        "a": "The mounting hole corresponds to the industrial standard, so that our tools fit on almost all professional socket welding machines."
      }
    ]
  },
  "welding-machine-50125-complete-set": {
    "seo_p1": "The table welding machine d50-d125 (Welding Machine 50-125 Complete Set) offers stationary precision for the prefabrication of large pipe assemblies.",
    "seo_p2": "It has clamping jaws, a lever mechanism for energy-saving joining and a digitally controlled heating element for absolutely exact joining pressures and times.",
    "seo_p3": "In the workshop production of manifolds or complex industrial assemblies, this machine eliminates human errors and maximizes processing speed.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What is the advantage of the stationary machine compared to the hand tool?",
        "a": "The lever mechanism allows an exactly linear, tilt-free insertion of the large pipes, which would be extremely strenuous by hand."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can small pipes also be welded with it?",
        "a": "Technically yes, however the machine is specially designed for the high joining forces of the dimensions 50 mm to 125 mm."
      },
      {
        "q": "How is the pipe fixed?",
        "a": "Universal clamping jaws with various inserts grip the pipe gently but absolutely firmly in order to guarantee a powerful, axial movement."
      }
    ]
  },
  "butt-welding-machine-90250": {
    "seo_p1": "The butt welding machine d90-d250 (Butt Welding Machine 90-250) is the high-end system for flangeless pipe-to-pipe connections in large format.",
    "seo_p2": "A hydraulic press unit, a CNC-controlled heating mirror and a precise pipe planer ensure a fully automated, loggable weld seam at the highest level.",
    "seo_p3": "For municipal main water pipes or industrial cooling water networks from 90 mm, this device is indispensable for carrying out certified and approvable butt welds.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What is the difference between socket and butt welding?",
        "a": "With butt welding, the pipe ends are milled flat and melted together directly without an additional fitting (socket)."
      },
      {
        "q": "Are the welding data saved for quality control?",
        "a": "Yes, the integrated CNC control logs temperature, pressure and time for each individual weld seam for later evaluation."
      },
      {
        "q": "Why is a planer integrated?",
        "a": "The planer mills both pipe ends absolutely parallel and oxidation-free before welding, which is strictly necessary for a permanent molecular connection."
      }
    ]
  },
  "electrofusion-machine": {
    "seo_p1": "The electrofusion machine controls the fully automatic welding process of electrofusion sockets by electrical resistance heating.",
    "seo_p2": "The intelligent microprocessor reads the barcode of the fitting via scanner and automatically calculates the exact voltage and welding time depending on the ambient temperature.",
    "seo_p3": "Essential for repairs in extremely narrow shafts, subsequent connections or underground installations where classic socket welding is impossible due to space constraints.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "How does the machine read the welding parameters?",
        "a": "Every electrofusion socket has a barcode, which the user reads with the connected scanner; the machine adjusts itself fully automatically."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the machine compensate for temperature fluctuations on the construction site?",
        "a": "Yes, an ambient sensor measures the temperature and automatically adjusts the welding time (longer in winter, shorter in summer)."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the pipe have to be peeled before electrofusion?",
        "a": "Absolutely! The oxide layer on the PP-R pipe must be mechanically removed in the welding area with a special peeling device."
      }
    ]
  },
  "welding-tool-for-weld-in-saddles": {
    "seo_p1": "The saddle welding tool (Welding Tool for Weld-in Saddles) is specially designed for mounting weld-in saddles on existing PP-R pipes.",
    "seo_p2": "It consists of a concavely shaped heating mandrel for the pipe wall and a convex heating socket for the saddle, both with high-quality Teflon coating.",
    "seo_p3": "It heats exactly the required area on the base pipe in order to fuse the saddle homogeneously and inseparably with the piping system.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Why does the tool have a concave and a convex side?",
        "a": "The concave (arched) side heats the round outer pipe, while the convex side brings exactly the saddle-shaped branch to melting temperature."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does one tool fit all pipes?",
        "a": "No, you need an exactly fitting saddle welding tool for each main pipe/branch combination (e.g. 63 mm to 20 mm)."
      },
      {
        "q": "How is the tool mounted on the welding machine?",
        "a": "It is screwed directly onto the heating sword of the K Aqua hand welding machine like a normal heating mandrel with an Allen screw."
      }
    ]
  },
  "drilling-tool-for-weld-in-saddle": {
    "seo_p1": "The special drill for weld-in saddles (Drilling Tool for Weld-in Saddle) is the precise preparation tool for saddle branches.",
    "seo_p2": "It not only drills the exactly required hole in the water-bearing main pipe, but also neatly mills out the edge area for the subsequent welding.",
    "seo_p3": "An extremely sharp and clean drill hole is critical so that no plastic chips get into the pipe network during the later welding of the saddle.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Why can't I use a normal wood or metal drill?",
        "a": "Standard drills tear the plastic and produce uncontrolled chips. Our special drill mills the hole and cleanly catches the chip."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the drill fit in a standard cordless screwdriver?",
        "a": "Yes, the drill has a standardized hexagonal shaft that fits into any standard drill chuck."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the hole have to be deburred?",
        "a": "No, the milling head of the drill is designed in such a way that it automatically prepares and smooths the hole edge for the subsequent welding."
      }
    ]
  },
  "welding-tool-for-repairing-plug": {
    "seo_p1": "The repair welding tool (Welding Tool for Repairing Plug) is a highly specialized attachment for repairing drilled pipes.",
    "seo_p2": "This conical heating pin specifically heats the interior of a damaged drill hole and simultaneously the corresponding PP-R repair plug to melting temperature.",
    "seo_p3": "It is the savior on every construction site to quickly and demonstrably tightly close accidentally drilled pipes (e.g. during wall mounting).",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "How exactly does the repair pin work?",
        "a": "The conical tool melts the drill hole. Afterwards, the also heated PP-R repair plug is pressed into the hole and fuses permanently."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is the repaired spot really safe?",
        "a": "Yes, it is not a mere bonding, but a molecular weld that withstands the same pressure as the undamaged pipe."
      },
      {
        "q": "Which drill diameters can be repaired?",
        "a": "The tool is ideal for typical drilling accidents (dowel holes) in the range of 7 mm to 11 mm."
      }
    ]
  },
  "repairing-plug": {
    "seo_p1": "The repair plug (Repairing Plug) is a solid PP-R pin which, in combination with the special welding tool, repairs drill hole emergencies.",
    "seo_p2": "It is made of the identical material as the K Aqua pipe system and fuses to an absolutely homogeneous mass when inserted into the damaged pipe.",
    "seo_p3": "Instead of opening up walls over a large area to replace pipe sections, the hole is simply welded; the repaired spot is then just as pressure-resistant as the original pipe.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What material is the repair plug made of?",
        "a": "It consists of 100% high-quality Polypropylene Random Copolymer (PP-R) Type 3, exactly like our K Aqua pipe systems."
      },
      {
        "q": "Must the plug be cut off after welding?",
        "a": "Yes, after the welding spot has cooled down completely, the protruding end of the plug is cut off flush with the pipe wall."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I use the plug when the pipe network is filled?",
        "a": "No, the water must be completely turned off on the affected line and the pipe must be dry in the area of the drill hole."
      }
    ]
  }

